Comparison rule: estimate the first integer low phase whose empirical exact-byte success rate is >= 0.95. This 95% value is a study convention, not a universal protocol requirement.
Per seed: 200 pre-generated seven-transition jitter profiles; uniform integer perturbation [-6 ns,+6 ns]; same profiles reused at all timing settings and by both methods; candidate low phases 1..8 cycles.
Runs: 30 seeds (20261115 through 20261144).
Observed boundary: 4 cycles for both algorithms in 30/30 runs.
Median transactions: fixed sweep 1600; binary search 1000; observed reduction 37.5% for this model and candidate range.
Evidence class: software simulation of a declared model. This comparison uses equal repeats per probed setting and reports total transactions; it is not a same-total-budget accuracy comparison and does not establish RTL, hardware, physical timing, or novelty.
